0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Python library for extrating geospatial extent of DOIs, URLs, files, directories, data repositories with multiple data formats and APIs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/TIBHannover/geoMetadata&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;geoMetadata&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;6 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;2&lt;br&gt;geoMetadata Plugin for OJS &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/GeoinformationSystems/optimap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;optimap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;4 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Geospatial discovery of research articles based on open metadata&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/GeoinformationSystems/janeway_geometadata&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;janeway_geometadata&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;1 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Geospatial metadata for preprints and articles publish in Janeway&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Hi 👋&lt;/h1&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I (he/him) am a postdoctoral researcher at 🌊 &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.geomar.de/en/&quot;&gt;GEOMAR&lt;/a&gt; with the 🌉 &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nfdi.de/&quot;&gt;NFDI&lt;/a&gt; consortium for Earth System Sciences - 🌍 &lt;a href=&quot;https://nfdi4earth.de/&quot;&gt;NFDI4Earth&lt;/a&gt;. I&#39;m working on projects to make research in 🗺️ geography, 🌍🌏🌎 geosciences, and 🗺️❤️💻 GIScience more open, reproducible, and discoverable. I think about both 🗃️💿 data and 🧑‍💻 software to achieve that and have a passion for 🎚️ metadata. I strive to adhere to 👐 &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_science&quot;&gt;Open Science&lt;/a&gt; principles and 📢 advocate for open reproducible research and open scholarship.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;⚙️ Projects&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;🌍 &lt;a href=&quot;https://nfdi4earth.de/&quot;&gt;NFDI4Earth&lt;/a&gt; addresses digital needs of Earth System Sciences in the German national research data infrastructure (&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nfdi.de/?lang=en&quot;&gt;NFDI&lt;/a&gt;) [2022-08 - ..]&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;🟩 &lt;a href=&quot;https://codecheck.org.uk/&quot;&gt;CODECHECK&lt;/a&gt; is an open community that introduces minimalistic yet effective code execution practices into peer review processes to make science more transparent and reproducible. [Co-PI; 2019- ..]&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;In the BMFTR-funded projects ⏫ &lt;a href=&quot;https://projects.tib.eu/optimeta/en/&quot;&gt;OPTIMETA&lt;/a&gt; and ☄️ &lt;a href=&quot;https://projects.tib.eu/komet&quot;&gt;KOMET&lt;/a&gt; we strengthened the Open Access publishing system through open citations, PIDs, and spatiotemporal metadata by developing plugins for 📄 &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/pkp/ojs/&quot;&gt;Open Journal Systems&lt;/a&gt; (OJS). [PI; 2021-08 - 2025-09]&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;In the DFG-funded project 🔭 &lt;a href=&quot;https://o2r.info/&quot;&gt;Opening Reproducible Research&lt;/a&gt; (o2r) we developed tools for increasing reproducibility of computational workflows in based on ✨ &lt;a href=&quot;https://research-compendium.science/&quot;&gt;research compendia&lt;/a&gt;. [2016-01 - 2022-08]&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;👍 Interests&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am interested in 🤔 improving the scholarly 📃 publication and 👯 communication process with new 🚀 information technology and 🔓 open research information — of course with ⚡ Open Source software! I completed my 🧑‍🎓 PhD &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4768095&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Infrastructures and Practices for Reproducible Research in Geography, Geosciences, and GIScience&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in 2022 in 👨‍🏫 &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/edzer/&quot;&gt;Edzer Pebesma&#39;s&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;http://ifgi.uni-muenster.de/labs/spatio-temporal-modelling-lab/&quot;&gt;Spatiotemporal Modelling Lab&lt;/a&gt; at the 📍 &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.uni-muenster.de/Geoinformatics/&quot;&gt;Institute for Geoinformatics&lt;/a&gt; (ifgi) at the 🏫 &lt;a href=&quot;https://uni-muenster.de/&quot;&gt;University of Münster&lt;/a&gt;. My publications, CV, memberships, and service are in my &lt;a href=&quot;https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0024-5046&quot;&gt;🟢 ORCID profile&lt;/a&gt;. Before academia, I worked as a consultant and research software engineer at &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/52north/&quot;&gt;52°North Spatial Information Research GmbH&lt;/a&gt;. Because reserach doesn&#39;t work without software anymore, I was a vice chair of the German association of research software engineers (&lt;a href=&quot;https://de-rse.org/en/&quot;&gt;de-RSE&lt;/a&gt;) and am a self-identifying &lt;a href=&quot;https://software.ac.uk/research-software-engineers&quot;&gt;RSE&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I enjoy playing 🥏 &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultimate_(sport)&quot;&gt;Ultimate Frisbee&lt;/a&gt; — &lt;a href=&quot;https://thegreatestsporteverinvented.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;the greatest sport ever invented by man&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and prioritise 👨‍👩‍👧‍👧.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;📬 Contact &amp;amp; more&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Find links to all my 🤓 profiles at &lt;a href=&quot;https://nordholmen.net/&quot;&gt;https://nordholmen.net/&lt;/a&gt; and follow me at 🦣 &lt;a href=&quot;https://mstdn.social/@nuest&quot;&gt;@nuest@mstdn.social&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;💬 &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:daniel.nuest@tu-dresden.de&quot;&gt;Get in touch&lt;/a&gt; if you want to improve the reproducibility of your research, maybe &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1008316&quot;&gt;using 🐋 containers&lt;/a&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
      <media:content url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1325054?s=96&amp;v=4" medium="image" />
      
